 "prespecified": {
  "our_time": {
   "choice": "The time of a method in a cell is the median over its solver seeds of the wall time of the call (build + solve). A run that is not certified within the limit (the gap of the stopping rule not closed, or the call ended after the limit) counts as the limit; the median is a bound (censored) when at least half of the runs failed.",
   "why": "§12 (2): 'у SCIP — 3 сида перестановок, значение ячейки — медиана'; (5): 'время за лимитом берётся равным лимиту и помечается границей'."
  },
  "published": {
   "choice": "The best published time of a cell is the minimum over the methods of the BCW table of the printed times (Table 3: Algorithm 3, CPLEX big-M, CPLEX MISOCO; Table 4: and Algorithm 3 with the in-out cuts); a printed '>L' counts as L and is a bound, and when every method printed '>L' the best published time is L and a bound.",
   "why": "§12 (5): 'лучшее опубликованное время ячейки (минимум по методам таблицы BCW)'."
  },
  "ratio": {
   "choice": "The ratio of a cell is our time over the best published time. It is a lower bound when our time is a bound, an upper bound when the published one is; when both are bounds the cell has no ratio, is left out of the summary and is listed (excluded).",
   "why": "§12 (5): 'ячейка, где за лимит вышли обе стороны, из сводки исключается и отчитывается'."
  },
  "primary_view": {
   "choice": "The verdict reads SCIP's times (view scip): at the sizes of the OR-Library ports (n = 31-225) SCIP is the exact representative of RQ2 (tuned.json, sizes 100 and 200; OA is the representative at N = 400 only), so the rule of the plan judges the baseline that stood in H2 at these sizes. OA (view oa, T3 only) and the better of the two (view stack: the smaller of the medians of our methods, the analogue of the best of the BCW methods) are reported beside it and do not enter the verdict.",
   "why": "§12 (2) names the stack (SCIP and OA) and (5) 'наше медианное время' per cell without saying which method of a stack of two; the entry of §12 of 2026-10-18 (before the run) fixes SCIP, the conservative reading (exploratory laptop timings of the agent, 18 runs, not registered, were seen before it)."
  },
  "excluded": {
   "choice": "A cell where both our time and the best published time are bounds is excluded from the summary (counted in n_excluded, listed with its port and k); it still counts as not solved by either side.",
   "why": "§12 (5)."
  },
  "summary": {
   "choice": "Per table and view: the median of the cell ratios (bounds at their values; n_lower_bound, n_upper_bound and median_bound say how far it rests on bounds) and the number of cells of the 15 solved within the limit by us and by the best published method.",
   "why": "§12 (5): 'Сводка — медиана отношений по ячейкам каждой таблицы и число ячеек, решённых в лимите каждой стороной'."
  },
  "rule": {
   "choice": "The verdict of a table is above if the median ratio of the primary view is above 10 (10 itself is not above). The two tables are judged separately; the overall verdict is above if either table is (the conclusions of RQ2 then carry the caveat of the baseline).",
   "why": "§12 (6): 'медианное отношение больше 10 — выводы RQ2 только про открытые точные методы с оговоркой о бейзлайне; не больше 10 — … в пределах порядка от опубликованного'; the plan does not say how the two tables combine."
  },
  "hardware": {
   "choice": "No normalisation to the hardware of the paper: raw ratios of wall-clock times.",
   "why": "§12 (4): 'нормировки по железу нет, это раскрывается'."
  }
 },
 "published": {
  "source": {
   "title": "A Scalable Algorithm For Sparse Portfolio Selection",
   "authors": "Dimitris Bertsimas, Ryan Cory-Wright",
   "arxiv": "1811.00138v5",
   "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.00138v5",
   "location": "Section 5.1, Tables 3 and 4, page 26"
  },
  "hardware": {
   "machine": "MacBook Pro, 2.9 GHz Intel Core i9, 16 GB DDR4",
   "threads": 1,
   "software": "Algorithm 3: Julia 1.1 with JuMP.jl 0.18.5, CPLEX 12.8.0 for the master problems and Mosek 9.0 for the continuous subproblems; CPLEX big-M and MISOCO: CPLEX 12.8.0 with default parameters",
   "note": "our times are not normalised to this hardware (the plan says so): the ratios are raw ratios of wall-clock times"
  },
  "setup": [
   "problem (34): minimise x'Sigma x/2 + |x|^2/(2 gamma) - kappa mu'x on {e'x = 1, x >= 0, |x|_0 <= k}, gamma = 100/sqrt(n); Table 3 has kappa = 1 and no other constraint, Table 4 has kappa = 0 and mu'x >= rbar",
   "rbar = r_min + 0.3 (r_max - r_min); r_min = mu'x_min, x_min = argmin x'(I/gamma + Sigma)x/2, r_max = mu'x_max, x_max = argmax mu'x - x'x/(2 gamma), both on the unit simplex",
   "data: the five OR-Library problems of Chang et al. (2000), n = 31, 85, 89, 98, 225",
   "Algorithm 3 without the second-order-cone lower bound; with a return constraint feasibility of the master is ensured by a cut on the assets with mu_i >= rbar",
   "Table 4, column algorithm3_inout: Algorithm 3 after 50 root cuts generated by the in-out method",
   "all methods on one thread; limit 300 s (Table 3) and 3600 s (Table 4)"
  ],
